    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d602">

                <pb facs="0661" n="653" sameAs="frus:frus1939v02/pg653"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">865.4016/155: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Italy</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Phillips</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Rome</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1939-03-10T19:00:00+01:00">March 10, 1939—7
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received March 10—2:25 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>83. My 81, March 10, 10 a.m.<anchor n="50" xml:id="d602-f1"/> Ciano confirmed to
                    me this afternoon the information contained in my 78, March 8, 1 p.m. with
                    regard <pb facs="0662" n="654" xml:id="pg654"/> to foreign Jews in Italy.
                    Furthermore, he said that this applied also to the German refugees. There will
                    be no roundup or imprisonment of any foreign Jews in Italy on March 12.</p>
                <p>He gave me very definitely the impression that the decision had been reached to
                    relax the anti-Jewish campaign.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Phillips</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
